/target
Cargo.lock.bak
*.swp
.DS_Store
.claude/

# Tauri ACL artifacts, decided rather than defaulted.
#
# COMMITTED, on purpose:
#   crates/pelican-shell/gen/schemas/capabilities.json      (540 B)
#   crates/pelican-shell/permissions/autogenerated/*.toml   (10 files)
# These are the *granted* surface — which commands the webview may invoke.
# For a tool whose whole claim is that it can do very little, that surface
# belongs in review as a diff a human reads, not in a build directory nobody
# looks at. A PR that widens it should be as visible as one that adds a
# dependency.
#
# IGNORED: regenerable, large, and about upstream rather than us.
#   acl-manifests.json is 70 KB and is mostly Tauri core's own permission
#   catalogue — permissions we do not grant. The two *-schema.json files are
#   122 KB each of editor autocomplete. All three are rebuilt by build.rs and
#   would bury the 540 bytes that matter.
crates/pelican-shell/gen/schemas/acl-manifests.json
crates/pelican-shell/gen/schemas/*-schema.json

# Impeccable working artifacts.
# Kept: mocks/ (the comps and their approval sidecars are the design record),
# build/spec.json + regions.json, surfaces/, config.json.
# Ignored: everything regenerable from those by re-running the scripts.
.impeccable/review/
.impeccable/questions/
.impeccable/build/scaffold/
.impeccable/build/comp-grid.png
